subproblem.statement:
Let α be a type with a σ-algebra and μ a measure on it. Let n ∈ ℕ and C ∈ ℝ. For m ∈ ℕ and t, s ∈ Fin n let A_m(t,s,·), A₀(t,s,·) : α → ℝ, and let h_m, h₀, H : α → ℝ. Write A_m(x) := (A_m(t,s,x))_{t,s ∈ Fin n} and A₀(x) := (A₀(t,s,x))_{t,s ∈ Fin n} for the real n×n matrices (Matrix.of). Assume:
(i) every A_m(t,s,·) and every h_m is μ-a.e. strongly measurable;
(ii) H is μ-integrable;
(iii) |A_m(t,s,x)| ≤ C for all m, t, s, x;
(iv) for all sufficiently large m (eventually along atTop), |h_m(x)| ≤ H(x) for every x ∈ α;
(v) h_m(x) → h₀(x) for μ-a.e. x;
(vi) for μ-a.e. x, A_m(t,s,x) → A₀(t,s,x) for all t, s.
Then ∫ h_m(x)·det A_m(x) dμ(x) → ∫ h₀(x)·det A₀(x) dμ(x) as m → ∞ (Bochner integrals). No measurability or integrability of h₀ or A₀ is assumed.
